  {
   "id": "QDkyyCpkFgAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2019-02-08T11:37:24Z",
   "subject": "Re: Two-level CFA and restriction of error variance of the between level",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0cm\">I sometimes get negative error\nvariances at the between level (i.e., Haywood cases) so a qualified constraint\nwould be useful for me, but I don&#39;t want to do it without understanding its\norigin.</span></p></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>If your items meet scalar (&quot;strong&quot;) invariance across clusters, that implies residual variances == 0 at the between level.</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fpsyg.2017.01640/full\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fpsyg.2017.01640/full&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792424293569000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1l6mCroT4126KjkHdP_uwN\">https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fpsyg.2017.01640/full</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Most of the estimates do not significantly differ from 0 (the one exception might be a Type I error: 1 out of 15 tests would not be a surprise).</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\"><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792424293569000&amp;usg=AOvVaw00ojjNSgRMCsX6suYJVoay\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
